You can control the brightness of external monitors using ddcutil on the command line.

1. Install ddcutil:
$ sudo dnf install ddcutil

2. Try to detect your monitors (you should see all monitors listed with model numbers for identification):
# if this doesn't work, try again using sudo
$ ddcutil detect

3. Check to see the current brightness:
# Use the numbers found by detect as your display parameter
# 10 is the VCP code 0x10, which is for Brightness
$ ddcutil --display=1 getvcp 10

4. Set new brightness levels
# Use the current and max values found by getvcp 10 as a guide for what you can safely enter
# The second parameter of the setvcp command is your desired brightness level, probably on a scale of 0 to 100
$ ddcutil --display=1 setvcp 10 50
